# 8d and 8n: the lead agent puts four things in front of the person, one of
# each form, and each is answered in the action pane the way that form is
# answered. The lead agent learns every answer from its wait, once the
# answer has settled, and never earlier.
orch: init
orch: run new "four decisions"
orch: need question "What is the shop called?"                    -> expect n1
orch: need choice "Which colour for the buttons?" --options green,amber  -> expect n2
orch: need signoff "The front page is ready to go live."          -> expect n3
orch: need todo "Renew the certificate before Friday."            -> expect n4

pane actions: 100x30
expect-row "What is the shop called?"
expect-row "[ Green ]  [ Amber ]"
expect-row "[ Approve ]  [ Send back ]"
expect-row "[ Done ]"
click "What is the shop called?"
key o
type "Reef and Rope"
key enter
await: n1 state answered answer "Reef and Rope"
click "[ Amber ]"
await: n2 state answered answer amber
click "[ Send back ]"
type "the prices are missing"
key enter
await: n3 state answered answer "send back: the prices are missing"
click "[ Done ]"
await: n4 state answered answer done
orch: wait --timeout 0                              -> expect "Reef and Rope" "the prices are missing"
clock +5s
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 5                   -> expect answered amber done
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 0
orch: status                                        -> expect "0 agents"
assert: n1 state used; n2 state used; n3 state used; n4 state used
assert: no event lost; no event twice
